    "title": "Driving fatigue a leading cause of U.S. semi-truck crashes, East Texas attorney says - NewsBreak",
    "text": "KXII.com\nwebsite\nTyler\nDriving fatigue a leading cause of U.S. semi-truck crashes, East Texas attorney says\nBy Emma Burns,\n1 days agoTYLER, Texas (KLTV) - In light of two separate semi crashes, one of them being deadly, investigators say the drivers at fault had fallen asleep behind the wheel. Federal law limits drivers to 11 hours behind the wheel after 10 consecutive hours off duty. They can’t work more than 14 hours in a day, and must take a 30-minute break after 8 hours of driving. Electronic logging devices now track those hours digitally, making it harder to cheat the clock. But according to Brent Goudarzi, founding partner of Goudarzi & Young, some are still finding a way around the law.",
